The ambassadors for the final were former Argentine international [[Javier Zanetti]], who won the Champions League with Internazionale against Bayern Munich in [[2010 UEFA Champions League final|2010]], and former Italian international [[Paolo Maldini]], who won five European Cups with Milan.<ref>{{cite news|title=Final ambassadors: Zanetti v Maldini quiz|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0225-0e91a4b1629a-72f21485ad38-1000--final-ambassadors-zanetti-v-maldini-quiz/|publisher=UEFA|date=5 May 2016}}</ref>

===Logo===
UEFA unveiled the brand identity of the final on 27 August 2015 in [[Monaco]] ahead of the group stage draw. The logo features the Milan landmark [[Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II]].<ref>{{cite news |title=2016 UEFA Champions League final identity launched |url=http://www.uefa.org/about-uefa/administration/marketing/news/newsid=2274925.html |website=UEFA.org |date=27 August 2015 }}</ref>

===Ticketing===
With a stadium capacity of 71,500, a total amount of 46,000 tickets were available to fans and the general public, with the two finalist teams receiving 20,000 tickets each and with 6,000 tickets being available for sale to fans worldwide via UEFA.com from 1 to 14 March 2016 in four price categories: €440, €320, €160 and €70. The remaining tickets were allocated to the local organising committee, UEFA and national associations, commercial partners and broadcasters, and to serve the corporate hospitality programme.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.uefa.org/mediaservices/newsid=2337164.html|title=2016 UEFA Champions League final ticket sales launch|publisher=UEFA.org|date=1 March 2016|access-date=10 May 2016|archive-date=7 June 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160607170925/http://www.uefa.org/mediaservices/newsid=2337164.html|url-status=dead}}</ref>

===Opening ceremony===
American singer [[Alicia Keys]] performed in the opening ceremony prior to the match, the first time the UEFA Champions League final featured a live music performance.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.uefa.org/mediaservices/newsid=2357630.html|title=Alicia Keys to perform at UEFA Champions League final|website=UEFA.org|date=27 April 2016|access-date=11 May 2016|archive-date=30 June 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170630225756/http://www.uefa.org/mediaservices/newsid=2357630.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> The [[UEFA Champions League Anthem]] was performed by Italian tenor [[Andrea Bocelli]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/022d-0e94745db678-78f35366c7ce-1000--andrea-bocelli-to-perform-before-final/|title=Andrea Bocelli to perform before final|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations|date=26 May 2016}}</ref>

===Related events===
The [[2016 UEFA Women's Champions League final]] was held two days prior, on 26 May 2016, at the [[Mapei Stadium – Città del Tricolore]] in [[Reggio Emilia]], [[Italy]].{{citation needed|date=June 2020}}

The annual UEFA Champions Festival was held between 26–29 May 2016 at Milan's [[Piazza del Duomo, Milan|Piazza del Duomo]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/022d-0e163586078b-e77e3a6095d1-1000--where-and-when-uefa-champions-festival-in-milan/|title=Where and when: UEFA Champions Festival in Milan|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations|date=18 May 2016}}</ref>

==Match==
===Officials===
In May 2016, English [[referee (association football)|referee]] [[Mark Clattenburg]] was chosen to adjudicate the final.  Joining him, were compatriots Simon Beck and Jake Collin as [[assistant referee (association football)|assistant referees]], [[Andre Marriner]] and [[Anthony Taylor (referee)|Anthony Taylor]] as [[assistant referee (association football)#Additional assistant referee|additional assistant referees]], Stuart Burt as [[assistant referee (association football)#Fifth official and reserve assistant referee|reserve assistant referee]], and Hungarian [[Viktor Kassai]] as [[assistant referee (association football)#Fourth official|fourth official]].<ref name="Clattenburg">{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0252-0cda5ce4af77-2ad7b028d355-1000--clattenburg-to-referee-champions-league-final/|title=Clattenburg to referee Champions League final|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations|date=10 May 2016}}</ref>

===Goal-line technology===
The [[goal-line technology]] system [[Hawk-Eye]] was used for the match. This was the first UEFA Champions League final to employ goal-line technology, following approval by the UEFA Executive Committee in January 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/35726091|title=Goalline technology to be used in Champions League final|publisher=BBC Sport|date=4 March 2016}}</ref>

===Summary===
Real Madrid dominated possession in the early stages of the match. Six minutes into the game [[Gareth Bale]] delivered a [[Direct free kick|free-kick]] into Atlético Madrid's penalty box, which found [[Casemiro]]. His goalbound shot was cleared off the line by goalkeeper [[Jan Oblak]]. Five minutes later, [[Dani Carvajal]] received the first yellow card of the match after a late tackle on [[Antoine Griezmann]]. In the 15th minute, [[Toni Kroos]] sent a free-kick into Atlético's penalty box, which was flicked on by Bale. In the subsequent scramble, [[Sergio Ramos]] touched the ball past Oblak to score for Real.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Grez|title=Champions League final 2016: Live|url=https://edition.cnn.com/2016/05/28/football/champions-league-final-2016-live-blog/|access-date=28 May 2016|work=[[CNN]]|date=28 May 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Real Madrid beat Atletico on penalties to win Champions League|url=http://www.espnfcasia.com/uefa-champions-league/match/447229/real-madrid-atletico-madrid/report|website=ESPNFC.com|access-date=28 May 2016}}</ref> Watching the goal back at half-time, referee Clattenburg realised that there had been an offside in the build-up to the goal and that it should not have stood.<ref>{{cite news |first=Alex |last=Kirkland |title=Real Madrid's Sergio Ramos offside on 2016 UCL opener - Mark Clattenburg |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37583492/real-madrid-sergio-ramos-offside-2016-ucl-opener-mark-clattenburg |website=ESPN FC |date=14 May 2020 |accessdate=29 August 2023 }}</ref>

In the 46th minute, [[Fernando Torres]] won a [[Penalty kick (association football)|penalty kick]] for Atlético after a foul from behind from [[Pepe (footballer, born 1983)|Pepe]]. Real Madrid goalkeeper [[Keylor Navas]] was shown a yellow card for delaying the kick. Griezmann took the penalty but his shot missed the goal, with the ball ricocheting off the crossbar. Substitute [[Yannick Carrasco]] latched onto a cross by [[Juanfran (footballer, born 1985)|Juanfran]] from the right to equalise from close range for Atlético in the 79th minute. The scoreline remained the same at the end of 90 minutes to send the match into [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]].<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2016/may/28/real-madrid-v-atletico-madrid-champions-league-final-live-san-siro|title=2016 UEFA Champions League Final: as it happened |date=28 May 2016|work=Guardian|access-date=31 May 2016}}</ref>

After a goalless extra 30 minutes, the game was settled by a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]]. Juanfran missed Atlético's fourth penalty, hitting the post, thus allowing [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] to seal Real Madrid's 11th Champions League title.<ref name=bbcsum>{{cite news|title=Real Madrid beat Atletico Madrid on penalties|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/35947318|access-date=28 May 2016|work=[[BBC Sport]]}}</ref>

===Details===
The "home" team (for administrative purposes) was determined by an additional draw held after the semi-final draw, which was held on 15 April 2016 at UEFA headquarters in Nyon, Switzerland.<ref name="drawSF_1">{{cite web|title=Draws — Semi-finals |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/draws/2016/2000637/ |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |access-date=15 April 2016 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160510145703/http://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/season%3D2016/draws/round%3D2000637/index.html |archive-date=10 May 2016 }}</ref>

