==Post-match==
[[File:Sergio Ramos desde el balcón de la Presidencia de la Comunidad de Madrid con la Úndecima Copa de Europa.jpg|thumb|Man of the Match winner [[Sergio Ramos]] holding the [[European Champion Clubs' Cup|Champions League trophy]] during celebrations in Madrid.]]

Ramos, who scored the opening goal of the match, became the fifth player to score in two Champions League finals. He had not scored in the competition since scoring the equaliser against Atlético Madrid in the 2014 final. Carrasco's second-half equaliser made him the first Belgian to score in a Champions League final.<ref>{{cite web|title=UEFA Champions League 2016 - Real Madrid-Atlético Report |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/022d-0e957c5979eb-37493cb53cd0-1000--spot-on-real-madrid-defeat-atletico-in-final-again/|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations|access-date=29 May 2016|date=28 May 2016}}</ref> Real Madrid coach Zidane became the first French coach to win the Champions League and the seventh person to win the Champions League as a player and as a coach.<ref>{{cite web|title=UEFA Champions League - News – UEFA.com|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/022d-0e90fc10974b-cb5bd86b8f7d-1000--who-has-won-the-uefa-champions-league-as-a-player-and-coach/|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations|access-date=29 May 2016}}</ref>

During the match, fans at an Iraqi Real Madrid fan club were attacked for the second time, bringing the [[Real Madrid fan club massacres|combined death toll]] to at least 29. In the aftermath of the attack, club president [[Florentino Pérez]] dedicated Real Madrid's victory to the fans that were killed and other Iraqi fans of the club, including others who have been killed by the [[Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant]]. Players had previously worn black armbands and observed moment of silence after the first attack.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://vestnikkavkaza.net/news/Real-Madrid-s-Florentino-Perez-dedicates-Champions-League-victory-to-Iraqi-fans-killed-by-Daesh.html |title=Real Madrid's Florentino Perez dedicates Champions League victory to Iraqi fans killed by Daesh |access-date=2016-08-27 |archive-date=2017-10-08 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171008030604/http://vestnikkavkaza.net/news/Real-Madrid-s-Florentino-Perez-dedicates-Champions-League-victory-to-Iraqi-fans-killed-by-Daesh.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>

===Reactions===
Zidane expressed his pride at being Real Madrid coach and winning the Champions League with the club as a player, as assistant coach and now as head coach. Simeone congratulated Real Madrid on their victory.<ref>{{cite web|title=UEFA Champions League 2016 - Real Madrid-Atlético Quotes – UEFA.com|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/match/2015789--real-madrid-vs-atleti/|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations|access-date=29 May 2016}}</ref> When asked if he would continue as the coach of Atlético Madrid, Simeone replied, "My plan is to think. That's all."<ref>{{cite web|title=Atletico Madrid boss Diego Simeone: Real Madrid 'were better than us again'|url=http://www.espnfcasia.com/atletico-madrid/story/2882273/atletico-boss-diego-simeone-says-real-madrid-were-better-than-us-again|website=ESPNFC.com|access-date=28 May 2016}}</ref>

Ronaldo told the media after the match that he had requested to take the fifth penalty because he "had a vision" that he would score the winning goal.<ref>{{cite web|title=Cristiano Ronaldo: 'I had a vision' I'd score decisive penalty for Real Madrid|url=http://www.espnfcasia.com/uefa-champions-league/story/2882202/cristiano-ronaldo-says-i-had-a-vision-i-would-score-decisive-penalty-for-real-madrid|website=ESPNFC.com|access-date=28 May 2016}}</ref> [[Luka Modrić]] told the media he was happy and proud of the win, and that the team had shown character until the end.<ref>{{cite web|title=Luka Modric admits he "feels sorry" for Atletico Madrid after defeat|url=http://www.sport-english.com/en/news/liga-bbva/luka-modric-admits-feels-sorry-for-atletico-madrid-after-defeat-5165972|website=Mirror.co.uk|access-date=29 May 2016|date=28 May 2016|archive-date=4 July 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160704160730/http://www.sport-english.com/en/news/liga-bbva/luka-modric-admits-feels-sorry-for-atletico-madrid-after-defeat-5165972|url-status=dead}}</ref>

